=== 5. GF(2^q) (lem:hist:charsum, thm:hist:gf)
q=2: max_G N(G) over all 625 partial G = 8 ; bound 2^q+2^{3q/2} = 12
Jensen step log(2^{2q}(2^q-1)) - 3q/2 - 1 >= 3q/2 - 2 for q=1..59: True
q=2: I(f;x1)=0.9009, I(f;x2|h1)=1.4859, I(f->x)=2.3868 ; notes' closed form (q-1)+log(2^q-1)=2.5850 ; 2q=4
q=3: I(f;x1)=1.9561, I(f;x2|h1)=2.7635, I(f->x)=4.7196 ; notes' closed form (q-1)+log(2^q-1)=4.8074 ; 2q=6

=== 6. Small arithmetic facts used in hist
log C(n,floor(n/2)) >= n - log(n+1) for 2<=n<3000: True
sum_{t=2}^{n}(t-1) = n(n-1)/2 for n=50: 1225 vs 1225
Lipschitz example: |log G-log G'| = 0.11103 <= 0.11542
sum_{i>=1} 2^{d-i+1} for d=10: 2046 = 2N = 2048

=== 7. prop:hist:lhg (LHG-odd construction): is the sequence consistent?
X=Y={0,1}, x_1=0, x_{i+1}=y_i, y_i=omega_i: first inconsistency at step 4 (input 0 gets two labels)
(even construction x_i=omega_i, y_i=x_i is consistent: identity function)

=== 8. prop:hist:sketchfails: P vs private-randomness simulator (exact)
P's loss = 1.0 bit ; private simulator's loss = 2.0 bits ; mixture of constants = 1.0 bit
